      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The alloy is subjected to HPHT treatment at 6 GPa and 1473 K for 2 hours.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11087546::rubric_card::000::3e3b5fbe93"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Discrete solid-lubricant particles such as MoS2 are introduced during processing.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "HPHT treatment forms a hierarchically patterned microstructure involving FCC and B2 phases.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11087546::rubric_card::000::3e3b5fbe93"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The FCC/B2 interfaces produced by HPHT treatment are coherent.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11087546::rubric_card::000::3e3b5fbe93"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The solid-lubricant phase will be uniformly dispersed at grain boundaries or phase interfaces.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The HPHT-induced dual-phase structure enables effective dislocation transfer.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The HPHT-induced dual-phase structure mitigates stress concentrations.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "HPHT treatment enhances both tensile strength and ductility in Al0.7CoCrFeNi.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11087546::rubric_card::000::3e3b5fbe93"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The incorporated solid lubricant forms a lubricious surface film during elevated-temperature sliding.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Formation of the lubricious surface film reduces friction.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The HPHT-treated lubricant-containing alloy will have approximately doubled tensile strength relative to the untreated state.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11087546::rubric_card::000::3e3b5fbe93"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The HPHT-treated lubricant-containing alloy will have approximately doubled ductility relative to the untreated state.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11087546::rubric_card::000::3e3b5fbe93"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Adding the lubricant will produce a lower and more stable friction coefficient across a wide temperature range than in alloys without the lubricant.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
